summary_text:
Need modify caller. Use ref palette if ref exists and has palette. But if ref MB differs moving, extraction may succeed and validation fails -> no palette. Maybe fallback to current if ref fails? For moving content, use current; but static current must align ref, so ref first. If ref palette valid but validation fails, fallback current would break? Validation ensures current matches ref palette within threshold; if fails because content changed, fallback current quantizes new content, fine. For static, ref works. Good.

Patch:
```
SScreenContentPalette sPalette;
bool bPaletteReady=false;
if bHasRef && ref pointer { Analyze ref; if size>0 bPaletteReady=true; }
if !ready Analyze current.
if Quantize... set flag.
```
Need ref chroma offsets. Use pRef pointers at same MB. We have pRefY etc. Do it.

